# License

This project is deliberately split into two licenses so that both the writing and
the code are as reusable as possible.

## Prose, diagrams, exercises — CC BY-SA 4.0

Everything in `book/`, `exercises/`, and the Markdown documentation at the repo
root is licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0)**.

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You are free to:

- **Share** — copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format
- **Adapt** — remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose,
  including commercially

Under these terms:

- **Attribution** — credit *Frontier LLM Engineering* and link back to this
  repository, and indicate if changes were made.
- **ShareAlike** — if you remix or build upon the material, distribute your
  contributions under this same license.

Copyright (c) 2026 Frontier LLM Engineering contributors.

## Code — MIT

Everything in `labs/`, `tools/`, and every code block embedded in the chapters is
licensed under the **MIT License**. See [LICENSE-CODE](LICENSE-CODE).

The intent is that you can lift any lab, snippet, or configuration into your own
work — including proprietary work — without the ShareAlike obligation.

## Third-party material

Configurations, numbers, and results quoted from published papers and technical
reports belong to their original authors and are reproduced here under fair use
for commentary and education. Every one of them is cited in
[the reference list](book/appendix/b-references.md). If you are an author and
want a citation corrected or a quotation removed, open an issue.
